      "title": "Differentiating a Radical Function Using the Chain Rule"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "752d548d-a0a0-57b8-8cbd-7de826dbee48",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $y=\\sqrt{-10-7x},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=-10-7x.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}={u}^{1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-1/2}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-7.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{-10-7x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "c75e26a5-a424-52c1-bb33-24eaab3df542",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "6b8baaa7-1ff5-5255-adf9-5ea2fbd86c5f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{-7x-10}}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "f31d39cc-b779-5de7-97ad-e0496ed34e5a",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{-7x-10}}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "8d17ebc7-68aa-585a-82b6-746c8198c052",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{-7x-10}}"
            },
            {
